The Security Council,
Recalling all its relevant resolutions on the situation between Iraq and Kuwait, including resolutions 660 (1990), 687 (1991), 1284 (1999), 1859 (2008), 2107 (2013) and 2621 (2022),
Reaffirming the sovereignty, territorial integrity, political independence and inviolability of Iraq and Kuwait, and the importance of non-interference in their internal affairs,
Welcoming the continued cooperation between Iraq and Kuwait, including through the tripartite mechanism and the International Committee of the Red Cross, and the progress made in locating and repatriating the remains of missing Kuwaiti and third-country nationals,
Commending the Governments of Iraq and Kuwait for their efforts to address the humanitarian and property-related obligations arising from Iraq’s 1990 invasion and occupation of Kuwait,
Welcoming the completion of the mandate of the United Nations Compensation Commission and the dissolution of the Compensation Fund pursuant to resolution 2621 (2022),
Taking note of the report of the Secretary-General on the implementation of resolution 2107 (2013),
Emphasizing the importance of full implementation of all relevant obligations, in particular with respect to missing Kuwaiti and third-country nationals and missing Kuwaiti property, including the national archives,
Encouraging continued constructive dialogue and confidence-building between Iraq and Kuwait on outstanding bilateral issues,
1. Welcomes the progress made to date and commends the continued engagement of Iraq and Kuwait, together with the International Committee of the Red Cross and other relevant partners, in addressing the issue of missing persons and missing property;
2. Reaffirms that the obligations of Iraq under the relevant Security Council resolutions, in particular resolution 2107 (2013), remain fully applicable, including the obligations to locate, recover and return all missing Kuwaiti and third-country nationals and missing Kuwaiti property, including the national archives;
3. Calls upon the Government of Iraq to intensify its efforts, including by providing full access to relevant sites, information and archives, and to continue to cooperate closely with the Government of Kuwait, the International Committee of the Red Cross and the tripartite mechanism, with a view to achieving further concrete progress;
4. Encourages the Government of Kuwait and the Government of Iraq to continue their constructive engagement and dialogue on all outstanding issues, including through confidence-building measures and with the support of the United Nations;
5. Reaffirms its commitment to the sovereignty, territorial integrity, political independence and inviolability of Iraq and Kuwait, and calls upon both parties to resolve any outstanding bilateral issues peacefully and in accordance with international law and relevant agreements;
6. Requests the Secretary-General to continue to report to the Security Council every six months on progress in implementing resolution 2107 (2013), including on the activities of the tripartite mechanism, and to include recommendations on how to accelerate progress;
7. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

